  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Fedora currently tries to compensate internally if something fails while committing a change to the foxml and/or datastream files.  This improvement would change that so the work occurs in a transaction.  Goals include: simplifying the compensation code (mostly in DefaultDOManager) and having greater assurance that, when things go wrong (part of the overall transaction fails, power goes out, etc), storage comes up in a consistent state rather than requiring manual intervention.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
